# Line-ending normalisation for the whole repo.
#
# There was no .gitattributes here at all until 2026-09-09, which meant every
# text file was at the mercy of each contributor's local `core.autocrlf`. That
# is not hypothetical for this repo: it ships installers/install.ps1 and a
# documented Windows install path, and Git for Windows installs with
# core.autocrlf=true by default. Meanwhile .pre-commit-config.yaml runs
# `mixed-line-ending --fix=lf`, which normalises the working tree while
# nothing normalised what git actually stored. This file closes that gap.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides text vs binary by content, and every
# file it calls text is stored AND checked out with LF, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, marked explicitly so no checkout can rewrite their bytes.
# Only the extensions actually tracked here are listed; add to this list when
# a new binary type arrives rather than pre-declaring types the repo lacks.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion. It deliberately does NOT use the
# `binary` shorthand (which is `-text -diff`): git already detects these as
# binary by content for diff purposes, so the extra `-diff` buys nothing, and
# keeping the attribute minimal means it says exactly what it does.
#
# .svg is NOT here on purpose: it is XML, it benefits from LF normalisation
# and from readable diffs, and it is covered by the `text=auto` rule above.
*.png  -text
*.pdf  -text
*.pptx -text

# The two committed MCP bundles. Already covered by `* text=auto eol=lf` above,
# which stores and checks them out LF on every platform, so this is not fixing a
# breakage. It is here because .github/workflows/lint.yml rebuilds these two
# files on ubuntu and compares them BYTE FOR BYTE against what was committed
# from macOS. `-text` takes git's text/binary heuristic and any future change to
# the rule above out of that comparison entirely, so a drift failure can only
# ever mean the source and the artefact really disagree.
plugins/mail/mcp-server/bundle/server.mjs -text
plugins/chat/mcp-server/bundle/server.mjs -text
